  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_CheminDesFichiersEml">Path to the .eml files</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_SertAuRejeuD">Used to replay a problematic message and to run acceptance tests, without a mailbox or a network.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_DossierEtDisposition">Folder and disposition</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_DossierSurveille">Watched folder</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_NomCanoniqueEtNon">Canonical name, not label: a label breaks on a localised mailbox.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_ApresTraitement">After processing</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_DossierDeDestinationSi">Destination folder (when moving)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_Conversion">Conversion</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_DelaiMaximalParPiece">Maximum time per part (minutes)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_DepasseLeConvertisseurEst">Once exceeded, the converter is killed rather than waited for.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_PieceNonConvertible">Unconvertible part</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_SubstituteProduitUnePage">Substitute produces a page carrying the reason, Skip drops the part, RejectMessage rejects the whole message.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_ConvertirLeCorpsDu">Convert the message body</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_JoindreAussiLesPieces">Also attach the original parts</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_TailleMinimaleDUne">Minimum inline image size (KB)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_EnDessousLImage">Below this, the image is dropped: it is a signature logo.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_ExtractionRecursive">Recursive extraction</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_ProfondeurMaximale">Maximum depth</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_NombreMaximalDePieces">Maximum number of parts</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_CesBornesProtegentD">These bounds protect against a crafted archive. Raising them without reason exposes the service.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_VolumeDecompresseMaximalMo">Maximum expanded volume (MB)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_TailleMaximaleDUne">Maximum size of one entry (MB)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_ExtensionsEcartees">Excluded extensions</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_SepareesParDesVirgules">Comma separated. Example: p7s, ics, vcf. Used to drop electronic signatures and calendar invitations, which have no business reaching the ECM.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_FormatDeSortie">Output format</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_ModeDeProductionDes">PDF production mode</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_FormatDuFichierD">Information file format</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_XsltAppliqueUneFeuille">xslt applies a transformation sheet to the canonical XML: this is what produces the exact structure an ECM expects, without shipping code.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_FeuilleDeTransformation">Transformation sheet</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_Parcourir">Browse</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_CheminSurLeServeur">Path on the SERVER. The button is only a typing aid and is relevant only when the interface runs on the server.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_ExtensionDuFichierProduit">Produced file extension (no dot)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_VideDonneXmlUne">Empty gives .xml. A sheet declaring method=text produces flat output: use txt, idx or csv depending on what the ECM expects.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_MiseAuPointPasser">Development: set the format to xml, look at the output, write the sheet against it, then switch back to xslt. Both formats produce the same input XML.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_GabaritDeNommage">Naming template</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_PolitiqueDeDepot">Delivery policy</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_EcritureAtomiqueFichierTemporaire">Atomic write (temporary file then rename)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_SansElleLaGed">Without it, the ECM may read a PDF while it is being written.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_ToutOuRienEntre">All or nothing across targets</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_UnEchecSurUne">A failure on one target rolls back deliveries already made to the others.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_FichierTemoinEcritEn">Sentinel file written last (empty = none)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_TentativesSurEchecTransitoire">Attempts on transient failure</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_DelaiAvantLaSeconde">Delay before the second attempt (seconds)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_DoubleAChaqueNouvel">Doubles on each retry. Too short against a restarting ECM, all three attempts are spent before it answers.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_Traitements">Processors</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_TraitementsMetierApportesPar">Business processors provided by the installed plugins. They run in the order shown, at the stages listed.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_AucunTraitementMetierDisponible">No business processor available. Drop the DLLs into the plugin folder and restart the service.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_PluginsRefuses">Rejected plugins</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_CesAssemblagesSontPresents">These assemblies are present but were not loaded: their processors are not offered.</s:String>
