  <!-- Service settings -->
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_CesReglagesNeSont">These settings are not reloadable while running. Any change saved here only takes effect after a full service restart, and capture is interrupted meanwhile.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_Service">Service</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_RepertoireDeTravail">Working directory</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_ContientLesUnitesDe">Holds the working units in progress, the processed-message log and the quarantine. Changing it LOSES the idempotence log: messages still in the mailboxes will be processed again, hence duplicates in the ECM.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_TraitementsSimultanesToutesBoites">Concurrent processing, all mailboxes together</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_BorneLeTravailReel">Bounds actual work, not the worker count. A hundred mailboxes can listen with four concurrent jobs. Raising it beyond the LibreOffice profile count achieves nothing: conversion becomes the bottleneck.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_RepertoireDesPlugins">Plugin folder</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_RetentionDuJournalDes">Processed-message log retention (days)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_AuDelaUneEntree">Beyond this, an entry is purged. Too short, and an old message left in a mailbox would be processed again. The value must exceed the time a message can stay unprocessed.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_Outils">Tools</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_LibreofficeSofficeExe">LibreOffice (soffice.exe)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_Parcourir">Browse</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_SansLibreofficeAucunePiece">Without LibreOffice, no office document is converted: Word, Excel and PowerPoint come out as substitution pages. Apache OpenOffice will not do, its soffice does not support command-line conversion.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_ProfilsLibreofficeSimultanes">Concurrent LibreOffice profiles</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_ChaqueConversionUtiliseUn">Each conversion uses an isolated profile. Two conversions sharing a profile block each other, which is why this number actually bounds parallel conversion.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_Qpdf">qpdf</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_RepareLesPdfQue">Repairs PDFs the reader engine refuses. On a real invoice flow this is a few percent of documents, which would otherwise be delivered without being merged.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_RepertoireDesPolices">Font folder</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_LesPolicesSontIncorporees">Fonts are embedded in the produced PDFs, which are archived for years. Depending on a system font makes rendering vary from one server to another.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_Maintenance">Maintenance</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_PeriodeEntreDeuxPasses">Interval between passes (minutes)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_MiseEnQuarantaineApres">Quarantine after (days)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_UneUniteDeTravail">A working unit unfinished for longer is moved to quarantine rather than deleted: it carries the original MIME, the only way to replay the message after a fix.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_SeuilDAlerteD">Disk space warning threshold (%)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_EnDessousUneAlerte">Below this, a warning is logged and displayed. Capture does not stop by itself: it will fail at saturation, which is far more brutal.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_Pilotage">Control</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_ActiverLApiDe">Enable the control API</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_LaDesactiverRendCette">Disabling it makes this interface unusable: it only talks to the service through that API. The setting would have to be re-enabled by hand in the configuration file.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_PortDEcoute">Listening port</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_EcouteUniquementSurLa">Listens on the loopback interface only. After changing it, remember to fix the address in this interface's connection settings.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_JetonDePilotageVide">Control token (empty = unchanged)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_ChangerLeJetonInvalide">Changing the token invalidates EVERY operator workstation already configured, including this one. It must be carried over into each interface's connection settings.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_BaseDeMetriquesVide">Metrics database (empty = unchanged)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Svc_ChaineDeConnexionSql">SQL Server connection string for long-term history. The dashboard works without it, over a twenty-four hour in-memory window.</s:String>
